From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtakasi <mtakasi@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx-ai-engine: Stop USER_EVENT1 column scan after first hit

The completion IRQ handler scanned every shim column even after
USER_EVENT1 was found and cleared. For wide partitions this adds ~100 us
of unnecessary MMIO reads per command when the event is on start_col.

Add break after clearing the event in both aie2ps_interrupt_user_event1()
and _aie2ps_interrupt_user_event1().

Signed-off-by: mtakasi <mtakasi@amd.com>
---
 drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-interrupt.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-interrupt.c b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-interrupt.c
index 0295b455d87f..111111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-interrupt.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-interrupt.c
@@ -980,6 +980,7 @@ static void _aie2ps_interrupt_user_event1(struct aie_partition *apart)
 		trace_aie_tile_eevent(apart, &loc, AIE_PL_MOD, event_mod->user_event1);
 		complete = true;
 		aie_clear_event_status(apart, &loc, AIE_PL_MOD, event_mod->user_event1);
+		break;
 	}
 	if (complete && apart->user_event1_complete)
 		apart->user_event1_complete(apart->partition_id, apart->user_event1_priv);
@@ -1257,6 +1258,7 @@ irqreturn_t aie2ps_interrupt_user_event1(int irq, void *data)
 		trace_aie_tile_eevent(apart, &loc, AIE_PL_MOD, event_mod->user_event1);
 		aie_clear_event_status(apart, &loc, AIE_PL_MOD,
 				       event_mod->user_event1);
+		break;
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&apart->mlock);
 	if (complete && apart->user_event1_complete)
-- 
